);\npackages/lhc/test/validation.test.ts:35:  if (!result.ok) throw new Error(`read-back failed: ${result.error.reason}`);\npackages/lhc/test/validation.test.ts:40:  it(\"TC-4.1: four invalidity categories, each rejected whole with a named reason\", async () => {\npackages/lhc/test/validation.test.ts:61:    const cases: Array<{ batch: MessageEventInput[]; reason: RegExp }> = [\npackages/lhc/test/validation.test.ts:62:      { batch: [unknownKind], reason: /unknown event kind/ },\npackages/lhc/test/validation.test.ts:63:      { batch: [missingKey], reason: /idempotencyKey/ },\npackages/lhc/test/validation.test.ts:64:      { batch: [serverField], reason: /server-generated.*eventOrder/ },\npackages/lhc/test/validation.test.ts:65:      { batch: [turnEndWithPayload], reason: /turn_end/ },\npackages/lhc/test/validation.test.ts:68:    for (const { batch, reason } of cases) {\npackages/lhc/test/validation.test.ts:75:      expect(result.error.reason).toMatch(reason);\npackages/lhc/test/validation.test.ts:203:    expect(envelopeProbe.error.reason).toContain(\"envelope\");\npackages/lhc/test/validation.test.ts:211:    expect(eventProbe.error.reason).toContain(\"event\");\npackages/lhc/test/validation.test.ts:212:    expect(eventProbe.error.reason).toContain(\"surprise\");\npackages/lhc/test/validation.test.ts:223:    expect(payloadProbe.error.reason).toContain(\"payload\");\npackages/lhc/test/validation.test.ts:224:    expect(payloadProbe.error.reason).toContain(\"surprise\");\npackages/lhc/test/validation.test.ts:238:    expect(emptyActor.error.reason).toContain(\"actor\");\npackages/lhc/test/validation.test.ts:246:    expect(emptyHarness.error.reason).toContain(\"harness\");\npackages/lhc/src/cli/render.ts:25:  reason: string,\npackages/lhc/src/cli/render.ts:29:    stdout: `${JSON.stringify({ ok: false, error: { errorClass, code, reason } }, null, 2)}\\n`,\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:4:You are the story lead for `03-readiness-sweep` on durable story run `03-readiness-sweep-story-run-001`.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:19:Path: /Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/03-readiness-sweep.md\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:26:The sweep: walk derivation state through owning-domain reports, requeue transient failures through owning-domain requeue, return a receipt; standalone and embedded default-on in compact.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:36:- `sweep(ref)` per tech design §Flow 3: `messages.report` + `turns.report` → bucket (ready / pending→in-flight / blocked / failed) → classify failed by the reason-code table (transient / permanent / **unclassified ⇒ permanent**) → requeue transient through owners' `requeue` → `SweepReceipt`\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:37:- The reason-code classification table (tech design §Spec Validation row 1) as data, not branching logic\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:38:- Compact integration: sweep runs first by default, `sweep: false` skips, receipt embeds `SweepReceipt | { skipped: true }` — replaces Story 2's `absent`\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:39:- Once-per-invocation requeue dedupe (structural: owner requeue's `already_queued` noop counts as in-flight)\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:43:**Dependencies:** Stories 0–2. **Hard gate, verify before story start (extended per design):** (1) Epic 02's requeue patch landed — live-work-only queue rows, no terminal-row collision; (2) the terminal-failure write path verified against landed code — exhausted forms persist a classifiable reason class (FC-0.4 proved the fixture side; this gate proves the production side). If the persisted reason is opaque, the named Epic 02 patch is: stamp the provider's `retryable` flag onto the failed form at exhaustion.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:48:- **AC-3.1**: The sweep reads derivation state exclusively through owning-domain report surfaces and requeues exclusively through owning-domain requeue surfaces. It performs no derivation, no model calls, and no direct writes to any derived form.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:49:- **AC-3.2**: The sweep returns without waiting on any queued or requeued work.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:50:- **AC-3.3**: Failed forms with transient-class reason codes are requeued; failed forms with non-transient reasons and blocked forms are reported and not requeued; pending/queued forms are left alone and reported as in-flight.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:51:  - **TC-3.1** (AC-3.1, AC-3.2, AC-3.3): Seed a thread with ready, pending, transiently-failed, non-transiently-failed, and blocked forms (fixture-manufactured states); sweep → returns immediately; transient failure requeued (work row exists, form pending), non-transient and blocked untouched and reported, pending untouched; provider fake observes zero calls from the sweep itself.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:52:- **AC-3.4**: A given form is requeued at most once per sweep invocation.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:53:  - **TC-3.2** (AC-3.4): Sweep the same thread twice without draining → second sweep reports the requeued form as in-flight, does not requeue again; exactly one work row exists for it.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:54:- **AC-3.5**: The receipt lists, by owner and kind: ready, in-flight, requeued, blocked, and non-transient-failed forms, with reasons for the failed and blocked.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:55:- **AC-3.7**: The sweep is callable standalone through SDK and CLI with the same receipt shape.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:56:  - **TC-3.3** (AC-3.5, AC-3.7): Standalone sweep via SDK and via spawned CLI → same receipt shape; counts and reasons match the seeded states. *(CLI leg executes in Story 5's process suite; the shared receipt schema assertion lands here.)*\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:57:- **AC-3.6**: Compact runs the sweep first by default; a skip option suppresses it; the receipt records whether the sweep ran.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:58:  - **TC-3.4** (AC-3.6, AC-2.7): Compact with default options → receipt includes sweep section; compact with skip → receipt records the skip and no requeues occurred; drain after the default compact → requeued form heals; next compact's view includes the healed form. *(The drain leg exercises Epic 02 machinery through the provider fake — the one sanctioned test-setup use of inference machinery; no Epic 03 operation touches it.)*\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:65:The sweep is thread-view's only *writing* interaction with other domains, and it writes nothing itself — every mutation goes through `messages.requeue`/`turns.requeue`. It is the repair half of the degrade-don't-block posture: compact degrades around missing material; the sweep is why the same material isn't missing at the *next* compact. This story also completes the compact receipt: Story 2's `absent` placeholder becomes `SweepReceipt | { skipped: true }`.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:69:Gate first — both legs verified and recorded in the story log before any code (requeue patch landed; reason-class persistence verified against landed Epic 02 code, with FC-0.4 as the fixture-side proof). Then the classification table as data with its own unit legs, then the walk/bucket/receipt as a pure function over report outputs, then the requeue calls, then the compact embed + skip flag. Red: `sweep` stub + compact receipt still `absent`.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:75:| `src/domains/thread-view/internal/sweep.ts` | report walk (both owners), bucket (ready / in-flight / blocked / failed×classify), transient requeue, receipt assembly |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:76:| classification table (in `sweep.ts`, exported for tests) | reason-class → transient \\| permanent; **unclassified ⇒ permanent**; single source, data not branching |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:77:| `src/domains/thread-view/index.ts` | `sweep` real; `compact` gains the default-on sweep step + `sweep: false` skip; receipt flip |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:84:| Flow: bucket rules, `already_queued` ⇒ in-flight, no waiting | tech-design.md L283 |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:85:| `SweepReceipt` shape | tech-design.md L334–339 |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:88:| Epic 02 report/requeue surfaces (the consumed contract) | ../02-derivation-pipeline/tech-design.md L255 (report join + requeue semantics), L356–368 (signatures) |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:94:| TC-3.1 | `test/view-sweep.test.ts` | five seeded states bucket correctly; only transient requeued (work row exists, form pending); returns without waiting (elapsed bound); zero provider calls from sweep itself |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:95:| TC-3.2 | `view-sweep.test.ts` | second sweep without drain: in-flight report, no second row (count by key) |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:96:| TC-3.3 (schema leg) | `view-sweep.test.ts` | SDK receipt validates against the shared receipt schema; counts/reasons match seeds (CLI execution leg → Story 5) |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:97:| TC-3.4 | `view-sweep.test.ts` | default compact embeds receipt; skip records skip + zero requeues; drainSettled → next compact includes healed form |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:101:Supplemental: **classification edges** in `view-sweep.test.ts` — unclassified code → reported `permanentFailed`, never requeued; blocked → never requeued (not a TC; pins the conservative default the classification table mandates).\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:103:Zero-provider assertion completes here across all five ops (the fake is in fixture scope all around the sweep — this assert is what keeps it out of the operation). Once-per-invocation dedupe is structural (owner noop) but asserted anyway — if Epic 02's requeue ever stops nooping, this is the test that notices.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:107:Buckets come from the *owners' report joins*, not raw form states: \"retrying\" is a report-level distinction (pending + queue detail), and the sweep must not re-derive it from `derived_form` reads. The receipt's `requeued` carries subject ids so TC-3.4 can follow specific forms through heal. The classification table starts minimal (the design's named classes); unknown codes landing in `permanentFailed` with their literal reason is the receipt's visibility mechanism — expanding the table is config-tier work later, not a redesign.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:111:No waiting means *no waiting*: any `drainSettled`/polling inside `sweep.ts` is a contract violation even if tests pass — TC-3.1's elapsed-time bound is the tripwire. The gate is a stop condition, not a soft check: if FC-0.4's distinguishable-reason-classes proof fails against production writes, the story halts and the named Epic 02 patch (stamp `retryable` at exhaustion) is surfaced — do not classify on string-matching `lastError` prose as a workaround.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:115:Sweep through `createSdk().threadView.sweep` and through `compact`'s embedded step; requeues drain through the real background scheduler (`drainSettled`) in TC-3.4's heal leg — the one sanctioned test-setup use of inference machinery, and it exercises Epic 02's production drain, not a shortcut.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:128:- [ ] Gate verified and recorded in the story log before first commit (both legs: requeue patch, reason-class persistence)\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:129:- [ ] TC-3.1–3.4 green; unclassified-code leg green; zero-provider assertion now spans pull, status, compact, sweep\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:152:| `test/view-sweep.test.ts` | default | TC-3.1–3.4 |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:155:| `test/cli-process-view.test.ts` | process | TC-5.4; CLI parity for all five commands (pull, status, compact, sweep, materialize) |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:168:| TC-2.3 | 2.5, 2.7 | view-compact | failed