{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba packages/lhc/src/tech-utils/work-queue/index.ts | sed -n '340,420p'\"","aggregated_output":"   340\t\n   341\texport type FailAttemptResult =\n   342\t  | { terminal: false; attempts: number; eligibleAt: string }\n   343\t  | { terminal: true; attempts: number };\n   344\t\n   345\t// Terminal failure: the form rows land `failed` (or `blocked` for source\n   346\t// damage) carrying the final reason plus attempts/last-error copied onto the\n   347\t// form's metadata, and the item row is deleted — one transaction (DD-1).\n   348\t// Form writes stay version-checked: if a mutation moved the source since this\n   349\t// item was queued, the stale failure must not stamp the rebuilt form.\n   350\texport function failTerminal(\n   351\t  db: DatabaseSync,\n   352\t  item: ClaimedWorkItem,\n   353\t  opts: { reason: string; formState: \"failed\" | \"blocked\"; attempts: number; now: string },\n   354\t): void {\n   355\t  db.exec(\"BEGIN IMMEDIATE;\");\n   356\t  try {\n   357\t    const update = db.prepare(\n   358\t      `UPDATE derived_form\n   359\t       SET state = ?, content = NULL, reason = ?, metadata = ?, gaps = NULL, derived_at = ?\n   360\t       WHERE subject_kind = ? AND subject_id = ? AND form = ? AND source_version = ?`,\n   361\t    );\n   362\t    const metadata = JSON.stringify({ attempts: opts.attempts, lastError: opts.reason });\n   363\t    for (const target of item.forms) {\n   364\t      update.run(\n   365\t        opts.formState,\n   366\t        opts.reason,\n   367\t        metadata,\n   368\t        opts.now,\n   369\t        target.subjectKind,\n   370\t        target.subjectId,\n   371\t        target.form,\n   372\t        item.sourceVersion,\n   373\t      );\n   374\t    }\n   375\t    db.prepare(`DELETE FROM work_item WHERE work_item_id = ?`).run(item.workItemId);\n   376\t    db.exec(\"COMMIT;\");\n   377\t  } catch (cause) {\n   378\t    db.exec(\"ROLLBACK;\");\n   379\t    throw cause;\n   380\t  }\n   381\t}\n   382\t\n   383\t// A failed run counts itself. Under budget and retryable: the row goes back\n   384\t// to `queued` with attempts incremented and eligibility pushed out by backoff\n   385\t// (min(base × 2^attempts, cap)) — retry is not a status (DD-1). At budget, or\n   386\t// on a non-retryable failure, the item is terminal: form `failed` with the\n   387\t// final reason, row deleted (AC-1.9).\n   388\texport function failAttempt(\n   389\t  db: DatabaseSync,\n   390\t  item: ClaimedWorkItem,\n   391\t  opts: { reason: string; retryable: boolean; now: string; retry: RetryPolicy },\n   392\t): FailAttemptResult {\n   393\t  const attempts = item.attempts + 1;\n   394\t  if (opts.retryable && attempts < opts.retry.budget) {\n   395\t    const backoffMs = Math.min(\n   396\t      opts.retry.backoffBaseMs * 2 ** attempts,\n   397\t      opts.retry.backoffCapMs,\n   398\t    );\n   399\t    const eligibleAt = new Date(Date.parse(opts.now) + backoffMs).toISOString();\n   400\t    db.exec(\"BEGIN IMMEDIATE;\");\n   401\t    try {\n   402\t      db.prepare(\n   403\t        `UPDATE work_item\n   404\t         SET status = 'queued', attempts = ?, last_error = ?,\n   405\t             claimed_at = NULL, claim_expires_at = NULL, eligible_at = ?\n   406\t         WHERE work_item_id = ?`,\n   407\t      ).run(attempts, opts.reason, eligibleAt, item.workItemId);\n   408\t      db.exec(\"COMMIT;\");\n   409\t    } catch (cause) {\n   410\t      db.exec(\"ROLLBACK;\");\n   411\t      throw cause;\n   412\t    }\n   413\t    return { terminal: false, attempts, eligibleAt };\n   414\t  }\n   415\t  failTerminal(db, item, { reason: opts.reason, formState: \"failed\", attempts, now: opts.now });\n   416\t  return { terminal: true, attempts };\n   417\t}\n   418\t\n   419\t// Cascade tidy (tech design issue 1): delete still-queued items for the given\n   420\t// (kind, sourceRef) targets, returning the deleted ids for the mutation\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
